---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { business } from "../data/business";
import { buildSchemaGraph } from "../lib/schema/graph";
import { images } from "../data/images";

const path = "/about/";
const title = "About Warrior Removals | Local Movers in WN1";
const description =
  "Warrior Removals is an independent moving company based on Standishgate, WN1. House, office, student and piano removals across Wigan, rated 5.0/5 on Google.";
const crumbs = [{ name: "About", path }];
const schema = buildSchemaGraph({ pageType: "webpage", path, title, description, breadcrumbs: crumbs });
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} {path} {schema}>
  <PageHero
    title="About Warrior Removals"
    lede="An independent removals company based in WN1, covering Wigan, Greater Manchester and the UK mainland."
    crumbs={crumbs}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Warrior Removals is a local moving company based on Standishgate in WN1, at the same
          pin as our Google Business Profile. We move homes, offices, students, pianos and furniture
          across Wigan and the surrounding towns, with crews who know the terraces, one-way streets and
          estate cul-de-sacs from daily work, not from a map on the morning of your job.
        </p>
        <p>
          The business is built around one idea: a move done properly, at a fair fixed price, by
          people who turn up when they said they would. We are not a national franchise or a
          lead-generation broker, when you book with us, our crew loads your belongings and delivers
          them to your new address. That matters for accountability, insurance and the simple
          practical question of who to call if something needs adjusting on the day.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our fleet is 3.5-tonne Luton vans, the right size for Wigan's terraced streets and
          tight corners, and large enough that most family homes move in one or two
          well-planned loads. Every van carries furniture blankets, straps, sack trucks, dollies and
          tools for dismantling and reassembly as standard. We do not hold an O-licence because our
          vehicles stay below the 3,500 kg threshold; that is an honest description of how we
          operate, not something we hide.
        </p>

        <h2>How we work</h2>
        <p>
          Every job starts with understanding your move: property size, access, parking, what needs
          packing, and if furniture must be dismantled. For larger homes we do a free survey,
          in person or by video, so volume and access are seen before we quote. You can also use our
          <a href="/moving-cost-calculator/">moving cost calculator</a> for a guide estimate first;
          the survey turns that into a fixed written price valid for three months.
        </p>
        <p>
          On moving day, the agreed crew wraps and loads room by room, secures everything in the van,
          and places items in the correct rooms at your new home. Optional
          <a href="/packing-services/">packing services</a> can be booked for the day before so
          loading is efficient. We work seven days a week, {business.hours.label}, including
          weekends at the same rates, important for tenancy completions and office relocations that
          cannot wait until Monday.
        </p>

        <h2>What you can hold us to</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li><Icon name="check" /> <span><strong>{business.rating.display}/5 on Google</strong>, read reviews on <a href={business.hasMap} rel="noopener" target="_blank">our Google profile</a>.</span></li>
          <li><Icon name="check" /> <span><strong>£50,000 goods-in-transit cover</strong> per vehicle load and <strong>£1 million public liability</strong>, written into <a href="/terms-and-conditions/">our terms</a>.</span></li>
          <li><Icon name="check" /> <span><strong>Fixed written quotes</strong> after survey, price, crew and timings agreed before the job starts.</span></li>
          <li><Icon name="check" /> <span><strong>Seven-day availability</strong>, {business.hours.label} every day, weekends at weekday rates.</span></li>
          <li><Icon name="check" /> <span><strong>Local knowledge</strong> of Standish, Hindley, Leigh, Atherton and the rest of the towns we work every week.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What we move, and what we do not</h2>
        <p>
          We are a household and commercial removals company. We move furniture, boxes, appliances,
          office equipment, pianos and the contents of homes, flats, student rooms and workplaces
          from one address to another. We offer packing, dismantling and reassembly, and long-distance
          moves anywhere on the UK mainland.
        </p>
        <p>
          We deliberately do not offer waste or rubbish clearance, house clearance, international
          shipping, storage, or single-item courier work. Some listings confuse moving companies
          with waste carriers. We are not a waste business and we do not take rubbish or unwanted
          items for disposal as part of a move.
        </p>

        <h2>Wigan, Greater Manchester and the UK mainland</h2>
        <p>
          From our WN1 base we cover Wigan town centre, Standish, Hindley, Leigh, Atherton,
          Ashton-in-Makerfield, Orrell, Billinge and the wider borough, plus inter-city routes to
          Manchester, Liverpool, Bolton, Preston, Warrington and St Helens. If you are moving within Greater Manchester or
          further afield, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> or call {business.phoneDisplay} for a
          straight answer on availability and price.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="media-frame sticky-side">
        <img src={images.fleet.src} alt={images.fleet.alt} width="720" height="540" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
